#[navbar]

#[section, $md:
    @../ (Developers) / Rust project builders

    # Create a project builder in Rust

    A project builder connects Moth to an application environment. This guide
    builds a small Wasm package builder, then explains source packages, Rust
    bindings, configuration, directives and runtime output.

    The compiler owns language semantics. Your builder owns its application
    contract and uses the public SDK to request validated compilation and
    output services.

    Read alongside @../../docs/project-structure (Project structure),
    @../../docs/packages (Packages) and @../memory-management (Memory management)
    for their source and lifetime contracts.
]

